{"book":9,"chapter":11,"context":{"chapter":11,"title":"Saul Rescues Jabesh-gilead","summary":"When the Ammonite king Nahash threatens to gouge out the right eye of every man in Jabesh-gilead, the Spirit of God rushes on Saul. He rallies Israel, defeats Ammon, spares those who had doubted him, and the kingdom is renewed at Gilgal.","background":"Jabesh-gilead, east of the Jordan, had close ties with Benjamin (Judges 21). Saul's summons with pieces of oxen echoes the Levite's grim message in Judges 19. The soldiers are counted separately as 'Israel' and 'Judah' (v. 8), a hint of the later split.","customs":[{"term":"Thrust out your right eyes","verses":"11:2","note":"A cruel mark of disgrace. The historian Josephus explained that a soldier's left eye was covered by his shield, so losing the right eye ended his usefulness in battle."}],"watchFor":["'The Spirit of God came upon Saul' (v. 6).","'There shall not a man be put to death this day' (v. 13).","The kingdom is renewed before the Lord at Gilgal (vv. 14–15)."],"connections":["Judges 19:29","Judges 21:8-12","1 Samuel 31:11-13","2 Samuel 2:4-7"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["וַיַּעַל","vaiya'al","H5927","Hc/Vqw3ms","and he went up"],["נָחָשׁ","nachash","H5176","HNpm","Nahash"],["הָעַמּוֹנִי","ha'amoni","H5984","HTd/Ngmsa","the Ammonite"],["וַיִּחַן","vaiyichan","H2583","Hc/Vqw3ms","and he encamped"],["עַל","'al-","H5921","HR","on"],["יָבֵשׁ","yavesh","H3003","HNpl","Jabesh"],["גִּלְעָד","gil'ad","H1568","HNpl","Gilead"],["וַיֹּאמְרוּ","vaiyomeru","H559","Hc/Vqw3mp","and they said"],["כָּל","kol-","H3605","HNcmsc","all"],["אַנְשֵׁי","'anshei","H582","HNcmpc","[the] men of"],["יָבֵישׁ","yaveish","H3003","HNpl","Jabesh"],["אֶל","'el-","H413","HR","to"],["נָחָשׁ","nachash","H5176","HNpm","Nahash"],["כְּרָת","kerot-","H3772","HVqv2ms","make"],["לָנוּ","lanu","H9035","HRd/Sp1bp","to <the> us"],["בְרִית","verit","H1285","HNcfsa","a covenant"],["וְנַעַבְדֶךָּ","vena'avdeka","H5647","HC/Vqu1cp/Sp2ms","and we will serve you"]],"x":[